/-!
# The census: residue degree `4` at `41, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 79, 83, 97`

At a census prime `p` (split in `B`, unramified in `Ω`), the decomposition image in
`Gal(K/ℚ)` is cyclic on the restriction of the absolute Frobenius `F`
(`Local.decomposition_range_unramified`). `F ∈ G_B`, and its genus label `v` is the vector of
Legendre symbols of the radicands at the prime of `B` below the chosen place
(`Local.exists_absolute_frobenius_split`, `Local.frobenius_label_of_split`), from explicit
square-class tables at both `p`-adic roots of `241` (`CensusData`; the chosen place is
not known). For both roots `S(v) ≠ 0` in `Q_B`, so `ρ_B(F)² ≠ 1`, while `F⁴ ∈ core` for
every `F ∈ G_B` (`Q_B` has exponent `4`). Hence `F` has order `4` in `Gal(K/ℚ)` for every
admissible `K`: `e = 1` and `f = 4` (`census_inertiaDeg`).

The tables are checked by `decide +kernel` (`censusData_valid`); they are generated by
`scripts/sqrt241/generate_census_tables.py` (square classes `2 c'` with
`c' ≡ nA + nB·(±(2a−1)) mod p`, `a` a root of `X² − X − 60`).
-/

noncomputable section
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

namespace UnitDistance.Sqrt241.Retained

open Tower Presentation Cut GroupData ProCGroups UnitDistance.PrimeCompletion
